WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.760
Let's go next to Justin from&nbsp;
Orange County, California.&nbsp;

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:12.240
Just to carry high, yes, I can. Hi, David.
I was just wondering what your thoughts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.880
were on Joe Biden's town hall yesterday and&nbsp;
saying that he wasn't planning on canceling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.840
the fifty thousand dollars in student debt.
Yeah, so we talked about this a little bit on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.640
a livestream earlier this week. I appreciated&nbsp;
that he was just being direct in his answer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:32.240
Biden never ran on canceling 50000 in student&nbsp;
debt. He's not pretending like he's going to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:38.160
And he just said, I'm not going to do it. Now,&nbsp;
some of the some of the reasoning he gave about,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.400
well, we want to do K through 12 stuff or this&nbsp;
or that. I mean, you can walk and chew gum at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:47.360
the same time. If he was determined to cancel&nbsp;
50 K and K through 12 funding and improvements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.120
I think he would be able to do it. So I&nbsp;
think that some of the reasoning after the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:56.960
fact wasn't wasn't great, but I was refreshed.
As I said before, you know, if Trump were to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.480
asked, will you do 50 K, Trump would say, well,&nbsp;
you know, we're thinking about a lot of different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.640
things, but you've got to remember that college&nbsp;
has really become indoctrination. And for a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.000
of people, they go to college, they come out, and&nbsp;
all of a sudden they believe all these horrible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.840
things like Cryin Chuck, Chuck and Crazy Nancy are&nbsp;
good people. And we got to vote for Crazy Bernie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.400
So I'm not so big on college necessarily, although&nbsp;
I went to Upend and got the best grades and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.720
you know, I did so great at the top school and&nbsp;
my kids went there. But, you know, 10000, 20000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:30.080
50000, these are numbers and we're looking at them&nbsp;
very strongly and we'll come back to that in some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.360
period of time. Like that would be Trump's answer,&nbsp;
right? Biden said, yeah, no, I'm not going to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:40.160
the 50 K, and that's direct. It's consistent&nbsp;
with what he said all along. He's not bamboozling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:45.280
anybody. So I appreciated the directness, the&nbsp;
honesty. I wish his policy were a different one.&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.480
So you stand behind the cancelation.
Personally, I don't know about full cancelation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:59.360
I have my doubts about full cancelation of all&nbsp;
student debt. I do think that the the reason I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:07.200
more partial to partial would be that we have&nbsp;
a situation where, sure, college is optional,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:13.280
but increasingly with more and more jobs requiring&nbsp;
college and the cost of college going up and up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:20.000
and up, it's it's not totally clean to me. Just&nbsp;
to say if you choose to go to college, then you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.760
should you know, it just that's it. You've chosen&nbsp;
and you should be responsible for the full debt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:31.520
at the same time to say everybody just gets&nbsp;
a full cancelation of all student debt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:38.400
I'm not there. So I'm for partial cancelation and&nbsp;
I've seen a number of different plans that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.120
structure it in different ways. I don't know&nbsp;
exactly whether I would put a dollar amount on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:49.200
it or a percentage or how I would do it.
OK, that makes sense. Thank you, David.&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:55.760
All right, my pleasure. A lot of meaty,&nbsp;
substantive questions coming in today.

